# Small talk (only when nothing else is left). {subject} the id (a like id, pet, place, lunch, exams, weather, weekend,
# school), {thing} its words, {like}/{likes} for likes (likes=yes when she really likes it), {pet} her pet theme.
# 2026-10-27: more lines; small.plain was the "nothing to say" answer and repeated too much.

@rule me.small
on me.small
- [So... {thing}, huh?|What do you think about {thing}?|Been thinking about {thing} lately?]
- [Hey, random question: {thing}?|Can I ask you about {thing}?|I was wondering about {thing}.]
- [Got any thoughts on {thing}?|What's your take on {thing}?]
- [Funny, I was just thinking about {thing}.|Do you ever think about {thing}?]

@rule me.small.weather
on me.small
when subject=weather
- [Nice weather today, huh?|It's [warm|chilly|cloudy] today.|Do you think it'll rain later?]
- [Did you see the sky this morning?|Perfect day to skip class, right?|The wind's crazy today.]
- [Feels like it's going to [rain|clear up] later.|The sun's finally out.|Is it me, or is it humid today?]

@rule me.small.like
on me.small
when likes=yes|no
- [Are you into {like}?|Do you like {like}?|What do you think about {like}?]
- [Ever tried {like}?|I heard you might like {like}.|How do you feel about {like}?]
- [Are you a {like} kind of person?|Quick question: {like}, yes or no?|Somebody told me you're into {like}. True?]

@rule me.small.place
on me.small
when subject=place
- [I like {thing}.|This place is nice, huh?|You come here often?]
- [It's calm here.|Do you hang out here a lot?|Good spot, right?]
- [Feels different here than in class.|I didn't expect to find you here.|Nice place to take a breather.]

@rule me.small.stranger
on me.small
when rel=stranger
- [Hi. I don't think we've really talked before.|Hey. Nice day, huh?]
- [Hey, you're in my year, right?|Hi! Mind if I say hello?|Hey there. How's it going?]
- [Hi. We keep passing each other, so...|Hey, I'm in your grade. Thought I'd say hi.|Hello! I don't bite, promise.]

@rule small.plain
on small
opens share,ask,tease
- [Hm, {thing}? I guess so.|{Thing}... sure.] [It's alright.|I don't think about it much.]
- [{Thing}? Funny you ask.|Oh, {thing}.] [I have mixed feelings.|It depends on the day.|Why, do you like it?]
- [Honestly? No idea.|Hmm, {thing}...] [Never really thought about it.|Ask me something harder.|I'd have to think about that.]
- [Oh, that's random.|Where'd that come from?] [But sure, {thing}.|I don't mind talking about it.]
- [{Thing} is fine, I suppose.|Not much to say about {thing}.] [What about you?|You seem more into it than me.]
- [Ahh, {thing}...|Mm, {thing}.] [It reminds me of something.|I had a dream about that, weirdly.|It's okay.]

@rule small.like.yes
on small
when likes=yes
opens share,invite,ask
feel smile
- [{Like}? I love {like}!|Oh, {like}! Don't get me started.|You like {like} too?] [I could talk about it all day.|It's kind of my thing.|Finally someone asks!]
- [Wait, are you into {like}?|Oh my gosh, {like}!] [We have to talk about this.|You just made my day.]
- [{Like} is the best, honestly.|Ah, you found my weak spot.] [I spend way too much time on it.|Don't tell anyone how obsessed I am.]
- [Ooh, now you're talking.|You know the way to my heart.] [{Like}, every day if I could.|Let me tell you about my favorite part.]

@rule small.like.no
on small
when likes=no
opens ask,share,tease
- [{Like}? Not really my thing.|Eh, {like}...] [But I don't mind it.|Do you like it?|I've never really gotten into it.]
- [I don't get the appeal of {like}.|{Like}? Hmm.] [Convince me.|Maybe I just haven't tried it right.]
- [Not a big {like} person, sorry.|I'm kind of neutral on {like}.] [What do you like about it?|It's fine, I guess.]
- [Ha, {like}? Me? No.|I tried {like} once.] [It didn't stick.|Wasn't for me.]

@rule small.pet
on small
when subject=pet
opens share,ask,invite
feel smile
- [{Pet}? Oh, you have no idea.|You want to talk about {pet}? Really?] [I'm kind of obsessed.|Everyone says I talk about {pet} too much.|Okay, so...]
- [Ahh, {pet}!|Don't get me started on {pet}.] [I could go all day.|It's my favorite thing.]
- [How did you know I like {pet}?|You've been paying attention, huh?] [I'm flattered.|Okay, I'll tell you everything.]
- [{Pet} is my happy place.|Okay, {pet}. Yes.] [You'd love it too.|Sit down, this'll take a while.]

@rule small.weather
on small
when subject=weather
opens share,invite,tease
- [It's nice out, isn't it?|I like this kind of weather.|It's a bit [chilly|warm|gloomy] today.] [Perfect for a walk.|I almost fell asleep by the window.|I hope it stays like this.]
- [The sky's so pretty today.|Ugh, my hair hates this humidity.] [Makes me want to go outside.|I'd rather be at home.]
- [I heard it'll rain later.|They said it'd be sunny all week.] [I forgot my umbrella, of course.|Let's hope they're right.]
- [Weather talk? Really?|Ha, the classic.] [Fine. It's nice.|It's okay, I guess.|You're bad at small talk, huh?]

@rule small.lunch
on small
when subject=lunch
opens invite,share,tease
- [Lunch? I brought a bento.|I'm thinking bread from the store today.] [Want some?|The cafeteria line is too long.|I'm already hungry again.]
- [I skipped breakfast, so lunch is everything.|The cafeteria has curry today!] [I can't wait.|Want to go together?]
- [I made my own lunch today.|My mom packed way too much.] [It's not great, but it's mine.|Help me eat it?]
- [I'm on a diet. Kind of.|Lunch is the best part of school.] [Don't tempt me.|Obviously.]

@rule small.weekend
on small
when subject=weekend
opens invite,ask,share
- [The weekend? I'll probably just stay home.|I've got nothing planned yet.|Maybe I'll go shopping.] [Why, did you have something in mind?|What about you?]
- [I want to sleep all weekend.|I have a ton of homework, sadly.] [Unless something fun comes up.|Got any better ideas?]
- [I might go to the station mall.|My friends wanted to go to karaoke.] [Maybe.|I haven't decided.]
- [Weekends go by way too fast.|I'm already counting the days.] [Plans? Not yet.|Want to fix that?]

@rule small.place
on small
when subject=place
opens share,ask,invite
- [I like coming to {thing}.|{Thing} is one of my favorite spots.|It's quiet here.] [It's nice to get away from class.|I come here when I need to think.]
- [I found this spot in my first year.|Not many people come here.] [Don't tell anyone.|It's kind of my secret place.]
- [{Thing}? It's alright.|It's a bit crowded today.] [I usually prefer the roof.|It's better in the morning.]
- [This place has a nice feeling.|I always end up here.] [Weird, right?|I don't know why.]

@rule small.exams
on small
when subject=exams
opens comfort,invite,share
- [The exams? Please, let's talk about anything else.|I'm trying not to think about the exams.] [Okay, maybe a little.|How are you doing with studying?]
- [I've been studying until midnight.|I haven't even started.] [I'm going to fail math.|Don't judge me.]
- [Exams are a scam.|At least they end eventually.] [Right?|Then it's vacation.]
- [I think I'll be okay.|I'm scared of the history one.] [Probably.|Wanna quiz me?]

@rule small.school
on small
when subject=school
opens share,ask,tease
- [School's school.|Same as always.|Classes are classes.] [The teachers are piling on homework.|I can't wait for summer.]
- [Did you see what happened in class today?|Our teacher was in a mood today.] [It was so awkward.|I almost laughed.]
- [I kind of like school, honestly.|School's fine when friends are around.] [Don't tell anyone.|Better than being home alone.]
- [I fell asleep in class again.|I forgot my homework. Again.] [Don't laugh.|It's a talent.]

@rule small.stranger
on small
when rel=stranger
opens ask,share,praise
- [Oh. Hi.|Um, hello?|Do I know you?] [Yeah, it's... nice, I guess.|Sure.]
- [Hey. You're one of the new boys, right?|Oh, hi there.] [I've seen you around.|Can I help you?]
- [Um... hi?|Oh! Hello.] [Did you need something?|Do we have a class together?]
- [Hello.|Hi.] [Nice to meet you, I guess.|I don't really know you yet.]

@rule small.cool
on small
when voice=cool|serious|proper
opens ask,share
- [{Thing}. Hm.|If you insist.] [It's fine.|I have no strong opinion.]
- [I suppose we can talk about {thing}.|{Thing}? Unusual choice.] [Go on.|What about it?]
- [Hm. {Thing}.|That's a topic.] [I don't think about it much.|It has its merits.]
- [You want my opinion on {thing}?|Fine.] [It's adequate.|I could take it or leave it.]

@rule small.shy
on small
when voice=shy|bookish
opens ask,share,praise
feel shy
- [Ah, {thing}...|U-um, {thing}?] [I... I like it, I think.|Sorry, I'm not good at this.]
- [O-oh, you want to talk to me?|Um... {thing}...] [I don't know what to say.|I-I'll try.]
- [Sorry, I get nervous.|Um, {thing} is... nice?] [Is that a weird answer?|Please don't laugh.]
- [Ah... yes, {thing}.|I-I think about it sometimes.] [Do you?|That's all, sorry.]


# Pesos de implementação: em cada lugar, primeiro os valores que mudam o sentido da fala. Biblioteca: livros
# (l_study), silêncio, prova, depois chuva (wet), depois a briga na cabeça dela (fight/{fightwho}); as falas compostas
# (vários valores juntos) vencem sozinhas quando tudo vale, porque somam mais pontos. Chuva: weather
# (clear|cloudy|rain|storm), wet, rainlater, outside, rainlover. Gostos como chaves: l_study, l_food, l_animals...

# ---- your lines: the weather as it really is
@rule me.small.weather.rain
on me.small
when subject=weather wet=yes
- [Some rain, huh?|It's really coming down.|Did you bring an umbrella?]
- [I love the sound of rain on the windows.|Guess nobody's going outside today.|The whole school smells like rain.]
- [My shoes are still wet from this morning.|Think it'll stop before we go home?|Rainy days make everything slower, huh?]

@rule me.small.weather.storm
on me.small
when subject=weather weather=storm
- [Did you hear that thunder?|This storm is crazy.|The windows are shaking.]
- [Are you okay with thunder?|I think the power flickered.|Nobody's going home in this.]
- [Some storm, huh?|The wind's howling out there.|Glad we're inside.]

@rule me.small.weather.later
on me.small
when subject=weather rainlater=yes
- [Looks like rain later.|The sky's getting dark.|Did you bring an umbrella? It's going to pour.]
- [Those clouds don't look friendly.|The forecast said rain this afternoon.|Feels like it's about to rain.]
- [Smells like rain.|The air's heavy today.|I give it an hour before it starts.]

@rule me.small.weather.clear
on me.small
when subject=weather weather=clear
- [Perfect weather today.|Not a cloud in the sky.|Sunny days are the best.]
- [Great day to be outside, huh?|It's warm today.|The sun's out for real.]
- [It's so nice out.|Feels like a day off, doesn't it?|Look at that blue sky.]

# ---- her answer: rain, by who she is
@rule small.weather.rain.gentle
on small
when subject=weather wet=yes tone=gentle
opens share,invite,comfort
feel smile
- [I like the rain, a little.|The rain makes everything so quiet.|It's nice, isn't it? The sound.] [It feels like the whole school is whispering.|I could listen to it all day.|It makes me sleepy, though...]
- [I forgot my umbrella...|My socks got a little wet this morning.] [Hehe, I'll survive.|I'm hoping it stops before we go home.|Maybe someone will share theirs...]
- [Rainy days are good for staying in.|I always want tea when it rains.] [With a book, maybe.|And a blanket.|Don't you think?]

@rule small.weather.rain.energetic
on small
when subject=weather wet=yes tone=energetic
opens tease,invite,share
feel pout
- [Ugh, rain!|Rain, rain, rain!|Boo, rain!] [Practice got cancelled because of it!|I wanted to go out at lunch!|I'm bored out of my mind!]
- [Did you see people running for the doors?|Somebody slipped in the hallway, it was hilarious!] [Rain makes everyone crazy!|Okay, that part was fun.]
- [I'm gonna jump in every puddle on the way home.|Wanna race to the gate in it?] [Don't judge me!|Loser buys juice!|Come on, it's just water!]

@rule small.weather.rain.cool
on small
when subject=weather wet=yes tone=cool
opens share,ask
- [Rain. Yes.|It's raining. I noticed.|...It's raining.] [I don't mind it.|Fewer people outside. Good.|It's quieter.]
- [The rain keeps people indoors.|Rain is honest weather.] [The halls are crowded now.|No pretending to be cheerful.]
- [I brought an umbrella. Obviously.|I checked the forecast.] [You didn't?|Unlike some people.]

@rule small.weather.rain.teasing
on small
when subject=weather wet=yes tone=teasing
opens tease,invite
feel smile
- [Rain, huh?|Look at you, all damp.|So, no umbrella?] [Want to share mine? It's small, we'd have to stand close~|Hair's a mess. Cute, though.|Fine, I'll rescue you.]
- [Rainy days are perfect for staying in with someone.|Rain's romantic, don't you think?] [Just saying~|Or am I the only one?]
- [If I get wet, it's your fault.|I'm blaming you for this weather.] [Don't ask me how.|You look like the type.]

@rule small.weather.rain.lover
on small
when subject=weather wet=yes rainlover=yes
opens share,invite
feel smile
- [I love the rain. Really love it.|Rain is my favorite weather.|Don't tell anyone, but I was hoping for rain.] [I went out in it at lunch.|It washes everything clean.|Everything smells new.]
- [Sometimes I just stand outside and let it fall.|Rain sounds like the world is breathing.] [People think I'm weird.|Is that strange?]
- [Want to go out in it with me?|Have you ever walked in the rain on purpose?] [Just for a minute!|You should try it.]

@rule small.weather.rain.outside
on small
when subject=weather wet=yes outside=yes
opens invite,tease
feel surprised
- [Why are we even out here?|We're getting soaked!|Talking about the rain while standing in it?] [Let's get inside!|My hair is ruined.|This is so dumb. I love it.]
- [Rain's dripping down my collar.|Everything's soaked.] [You too, huh?|Let's find a roof.]
- [Out here in this?|Ah, it's getting heavier!] [Come on, under there!|Run!]

@rule small.weather.storm
on small
when subject=weather weather=storm
opens comfort,share,tease
feel worried
- [Did you hear that thunder?|The lights flickered just now!|This storm is scary.] [I hate thunder...|Stay close for a bit?|I'm fine. Totally fine.]
- [The trains might stop if this keeps up.|They might send everyone home.] [How would I even get home?|I hope so.]
- [The wind's so loud.|Lightning hit somewhere close.] [I jumped!|Did you see the flash?]

@rule small.weather.later
on small
when subject=weather rainlater=yes
opens share,invite
- [It's going to pour later.|They said rain this afternoon.|The sky's so dark.] [I hope I make it home first.|I brought an umbrella, just in case.|Ugh, and I have practice.]
- [Smells like rain.|My knee always knows when it's going to rain.] [Weird, right?|Grandma says the same thing.]
- [Let's hope it holds until after school.|Clouds like that mean business.] [Fingers crossed.|We'll see.]

@rule small.weather.cloudy
on small
when subject=weather weather=cloudy
opens share,ask
- [It's gray today.|Cloudy days are kind of nice.|The sun's hiding.] [Easier on the eyes.|Makes me lazy.|I don't mind it.]
- [Can't decide if it'll rain.|The sky can't make up its mind.] [Neither can I, about most things.|Typical.]
- [Gloomy weather, gloomy mood.|Cloudy. Like my brain today.] [Hehe.|Don't mind me.]

@rule small.weather.clear
on small
when subject=weather weather=clear
opens invite,share
feel smile
- [It's so nice out!|Perfect weather.|The sun feels great.] [We should go outside.|I almost skipped class to enjoy it.|Days like this are rare.]
- [Not a single cloud.|Even the teachers look happy today.] [Let's eat outside!|It's that kind of day.]
- [Sunny days make me want to do something fun.|I sat by the window all morning.] [Got any ideas?|Totally worth it.]

# ---- the library: books first, then the quiet and the exams, then the rain, then a fight on her mind
@rule small.place.library.books.rain.fight
on small
when subject=place placeid=library l_study=yes wet=yes fight=yes
opens comfort,ask,share
feel shy
- [I came here to read with the rain on the windows...|The library sounds different when it rains.|I like reading while it rains.] [It helps me stop thinking about {fightwho}.|Then I forget about the thing with {fightwho}. Almost.|It's the only place I don't think about the fight with {fightwho}.]
- [Rain, a good book, and no {fightwho}.|I needed somewhere quiet after what happened with {fightwho}.] [That's all I want today.|The rain kind of covers everything up.]
- [Is it weird that the rain makes it easier?|Everything feels farther away in here when it rains.] [Even {fightwho}.|Even that stupid fight.]

@rule small.place.library.books.rain
on small
when subject=place placeid=library l_study=yes wet=yes
opens share,invite
feel smile
- [Rain outside, a book in here.|Reading while it rains is the best.|Do you hear the rain on the windows?] [Perfect afternoon.|I could stay until they lock the doors.|It's like a soundtrack.]
- [I always come to the library on rainy days.|The best seat is by the window when it rains.] [It's tradition.|I got here first.]
- [Rain makes the pages smell older.|Rainy days are reading days.] [I know that sounds weird.|That's the rule.]

@rule small.place.library.books.fight
on small
when subject=place placeid=library l_study=yes fight=yes
opens comfort,ask
feel sad
- [I came here to hide in a book.|Books don't argue with you.|Reading helps when people are... complicated.] [After what happened with {fightwho}...|{Fightwho} and I aren't talking right now.]
- [I keep reading the same page.|I can't focus.] [I keep thinking about {fightwho}.|Stupid fight with {fightwho}.]
- [The library's the one place {fightwho} never comes.|It's quiet. I needed quiet.] [That's why I'm here.|You can stay, though.]

@rule small.place.library.books.exam
on small
when subject=place placeid=library l_study=yes exam=yes
opens ask,share
feel serious
- [Exams are coming. I'm prepared. Mostly.|I've read everything twice.|Studying here is the only way I focus.] [Want to quiz me?|You should study too.|Don't distract me. ...Okay, a little.]
- [The library's full of panicking people this week.|Every seat's taken during exam week.] [I came early to get this one.|Lucky me.]
- [I made flash cards for the exam.|I'm on chapter seven.] [Want to borrow some?|How far are you?]

@rule small.place.library.books
on small
when subject=place placeid=library l_study=yes
opens share,invite,ask
feel smile
- [I love it here.|The library is my favorite place in school.|Books, quiet, nobody yelling.] [What more do you need?|I'm here every day.|I come here every chance I get.]
- [Have you read anything good lately?|They got some new books this week.] [I'll lend you one.|I already borrowed three.]
- [The smell of old books is the best.|I could live in this library.] [Don't laugh!|Seriously.]
- [I'm halfway through a really good novel.|The librarian knows my name now.] [I can't put it down.|That's how often I'm here.]

@rule small.place.library.nobooks
on small
when subject=place placeid=library l_study!=yes
opens tease,ask
- [I don't really come here to read.|The library's... quiet.|Honestly? It's a good place to nap.] [Don't tell the librarian.|Too quiet, maybe.|It's warm, at least.]
- [Books aren't really my thing.|I only came because it's the one quiet place.] [Shh, don't judge.|Is that bad?]
- [I'm hiding from my homework. In the library. Ironic, huh?|I got dragged here.] [Don't laugh.|By a friend.]

@rule small.place.library.rain
on small
when subject=place placeid=library wet=yes
opens share,invite
- [Everyone's in the library because of the rain.|The rain sounds nice from in here.|It's so crowded today.] [It's never this full.|At least it's dry.|Too many people.]
- [Rain on the windows. Library smell.|The library's cozy on rainy days.] [Not bad.|I get it now.]
- [I came in to get away from the rain.|The rain drove me in here.] [Might as well read something.|I don't even like books.]

# ---- the classroom: the time of day and the exams, then the rain at the windows
@rule small.place.classroom.rain
on small
when subject=place placeid=classroom wet=yes
opens share,tease
- [Watching the rain from class is my hobby.|The windows are all fogged up.|Listen to it hit the glass.] [Better than the lesson.|Someone drew a heart on it.|Kind of relaxing.]
- [Nobody wants to go outside.|The classroom's packed because of the rain.] [So loud in here.|Everyone eats inside now.]
- [I'm staring out the window again.|Rainy classroom, sleepy classroom.] [Don't tell the teacher.|I almost dozed off.]

@rule small.place.classroom.exam
on small
when subject=place placeid=classroom exam=yes
opens ask,comfort
feel worried
- [The classroom feels like a prison during exams.|Everyone's so tense in here.|Exam week. In this room. Again.] [I can't breathe.|Even the class clown is quiet.|Ugh.]
- [Do you think we'll pass?|I studied until two.] [Tell me we'll pass.|I'm running on nothing.]
- [I keep looking at the clock.|This desk has seen too many exams.] [Is it over yet?|So many doodles.]

@rule small.place.classroom.lunch
on small
when subject=place placeid=classroom period=lunch
opens invite,share
- [Eating in the classroom is cozier.|Lunch at your desk is underrated.|Everyone pushes their desks together at lunch.] [No lines, either.|Want to join us?|It's the best part.]
- [The classroom smells like everyone's bento.|Somebody brought curry again.] [I'm so hungry now.|The whole room smells like it.]
- [Lunch break is too short.|I always eat too fast.] [Why is it so short?|Then I'm hungry again by fifth period.]

# ---- the cafeteria: food first
@rule small.place.cafeteria.food
on small
when subject=place placeid=cafeteria l_food=yes
opens invite,share
feel smile
- [The cafeteria is my happy place.|I already know today's menu.|I'd come here even if I wasn't hungry.] [Don't judge me.|The katsu curry is calling.|Food is life.]
- [Have you tried the special?|The new set meal is so good.] [Get it. Trust me.|I had it twice this week.]
- [I eat first and think later.|Second helpings are a right.] [That's my motto.|Fight me.]

@rule small.place.cafeteria.sweets
on small
when subject=place placeid=cafeteria l_sweets=yes
opens invite,tease
feel smile
- [They have pudding today!|Dessert first. Always.|I came for the melon bread, honestly.] [I almost cried.|Life's short.|It sells out so fast.]
- [Want to split a parfait?|The store has new sweets.] [Half for you, half for me. Mostly me.|I'm buying all of them.]
- [Sweets fix everything.|My bag is half snacks.] [Science.|Want one?]

@rule small.place.cafeteria.rain
on small
when subject=place placeid=cafeteria wet=yes
opens share,tease
- [Everybody's eating in here because of the rain.|It's so packed today.|No seats left, thanks to the rain.] [It's like a festival.|We could squeeze in.|Ugh.]
- [The windows are all steamed up.|Hot soup on a rainy day is perfect.] [Smells good in here, though.|Want some?]
- [The rain made the line twice as long.|I almost slipped on the wet floor.] [Worth it.|Carry my tray?]

# ---- the rooftop and the courtyard: outside, so the weather weighs a lot
@rule small.place.rooftop.rain
on small
when subject=place placeid=rooftop wet=yes
opens invite,tease,comfort
feel surprised
- [Why are we up here in the rain?|The rooftop's all ours. Nobody else is crazy enough.|We're getting soaked!] [Hehe.|Kinda nice, though.|I don't even care anymore.]
- [The city looks blurry from up here.|You can see the rain coming over the rooftops.] [Pretty, right?|Look!]
- [We should go in before we catch a cold.|My shoes are full of water.] [Five more minutes.|Okay, maybe now.]

@rule small.place.rooftop.lover
on small
when subject=place placeid=rooftop wet=yes rainlover=yes
opens invite,share
feel smile
- [I come up here when it rains. On purpose.|Rain on the rooftop is the best.|Nobody comes up here when it rains. It's mine.] [Don't tell anyone.|Close your eyes. Listen.|Well, ours now.]
- [The rain feels different up here.|I like letting it fall on my face.] [Closer to the sky.|Try it.]
- [Everyone runs from the rain. I don't get it.|Rain on the rooftop is my secret.] [It's just water.|Now it's yours too.]

@rule small.place.rooftop.clear
on small
when subject=place placeid=rooftop weather=clear
opens invite,share
feel smile
- [What a view.|You can see the whole town from here.|The wind feels so nice up here.] [I come here to think.|Look, there's the station.|Don't you love it?]
- [Perfect day for the rooftop.|The sky's so blue today.] [Lunch up here tomorrow?|I could nap right here.]
- [This is my secret spot. Well, not so secret now.|The breeze is the best part.] [Don't tell anyone.|Feel that?]

@rule small.place.courtyard.rain
on small
when subject=place placeid=courtyard wet=yes
opens invite,tease
- [The courtyard's empty in the rain.|All the benches are soaked.|Nobody out here but us.] [Kind of peaceful.|No sitting today.|Lucky us?]
- [The flowers look happy, at least.|Listen to the rain on the leaves.] [Someone has to be.|Pretty.]
- [We should get under the roof.|My umbrella's tiny.] [Come here.|Squeeze in.]

@rule small.place.courtyard.animals
on small
when subject=place placeid=courtyard l_animals=yes
opens invite,share
feel smile
- [There's a cat that sleeps under that bench.|I saw the stray cat again this morning.|Have you met the courtyard cat?] [I call her Mochi.|She let me pet her!|She's so fluffy.]
- [The birds come down when it's quiet.|I sneak bread out for the sparrows.] [Look, there.|Don't tell the teachers.]
- [The courtyard cat has a boyfriend now.|I bring treats for the cat on Fridays.] [A big orange one.|She waits for me.]

# ---- the field, the gym and the pool: sports first, then the weather
@rule small.place.field.sports
on small
when subject=place placeid=field clubkind=sports
opens invite,tease
feel smile
- [I practically live on this field.|Practice is my favorite part of the day.|Want to run a lap with me?] [Smell that grass!|No class can beat it.|Bet you can't keep up!]
- [Coach is making us run extra this week.|We have a match coming up.] [My legs are dead.|Come cheer for us!]
- [Some days I'm out here before anyone else.|The field at sunset is the best.] [Just me and the track.|Trust me.]

@rule small.place.field.rain
on small
when subject=place placeid=field wet=yes
opens tease,invite
- [The field is all mud now.|Practice is cancelled. Thanks, rain.|Look at those puddles.] [My cleats are ruined.|I'm so bored!|Wanna jump in one?]
- [We're running drills in the hallway instead.|The track's flooded.] [Everyone keeps slipping.|Ridiculous.]
- [Nobody's out here but us idiots.|Running in the rain is kind of fun, though.] [Proud of it.|Don't tell anyone.]

@rule small.place.gym.rain
on small
when subject=place placeid=gym wet=yes
opens invite,tease
- [Every club's crammed in the gym because of the rain.|The gym's chaos today.|Three teams, one gym.] [We had to share half a court.|Balls flying everywhere.|Watch your head.]
- [The roof's so loud when it rains.|Rain on the gym roof sounds like drums.] [You can't hear the coach.|Kind of cool.]
- [Outdoor clubs are stuck in here with us.|The track team is running laps around the gym.] [Hehe.|Dizzy just watching.]

@rule small.place.gym.exercise
on small
when subject=place placeid=gym l_exercise=yes
opens invite,tease
feel smile
- [I love the gym.|The gym's where I feel most like me.|Want to shoot some hoops?] [Sweat is just weakness leaving.|No thinking, just moving.|I'll go easy on you.]
- [I come here even on off days.|Free throws relax me.] [Is that weird?|Weird, right?]
- [Race you to the wall!|Let's see how many push-ups you can do.] [Loser buys drinks!|Bet I can do more.]

@rule small.place.pool.rain
on small
when subject=place placeid=pool wet=yes
opens tease,invite
- [Swimming in the rain is weird. You're wet either way.|Pool's closed when it thunders.|The rain makes little circles on the water.] [Hehe.|Rules are rules.|Pretty, right?]
- [Nobody's swimming today.|The pool looks so sad in the rain.] [Just us.|Poor pool.]
- [Rain or not, I'm wet anyway.|Coach still made us swim.] [Might as well.|Rain is nothing.]

@rule small.place.pool.clear
on small
when subject=place placeid=pool weather=clear
opens invite,tease
feel smile
- [Perfect pool weather.|The water's so blue today.|Want to swim? I'm kidding. Mostly.] [I wish I could jump in right now.|Sparkly.|You're blushing.]
- [Summer's the best because of the pool.|The sun on the water is so pretty.] [Don't you think?|Look.]
- [I could float here all day.|The pool smells like summer.] [Lucky swimmers.|Chlorine and sunscreen.]

# ---- the infirmary: how she feels, and what she's hiding from
@rule small.place.infirmary.fight
on small
when subject=place placeid=infirmary fight=yes
opens comfort,ask
feel sad
- [I said I had a headache. I don't.|I'm not sick. I just didn't want to see {fightwho}.|It's quiet here. Nobody asks questions.] [I just needed a break.|Please don't tell anyone.|Except you, apparently.]
- [The nurse let me lie down for a while.|I've been staring at the ceiling.] [I didn't want to go back to class.|Thinking about {fightwho}.]
- [Hiding in the infirmary is pathetic, right?|It's easier than facing {fightwho}.] [Don't answer that.|For now.]

@rule small.place.infirmary.sleepy
on small
when subject=place placeid=infirmary mood=sleepy
opens tease,comfort
feel shy
- [The infirmary beds are so comfy...|I'm just resting my eyes.|Five more minutes.] [Shh.|Don't tell.|Please?]
- [I didn't sleep at all last night.|The nurse took pity on me.] [Zombie mode.|Lucky.]
- [This pillow is better than mine at home.|Can you wake me before the bell?] [Seriously.|Thanks.]

# ---- the club room: her club first
@rule small.place.clubroom.club
on small
when subject=place placeid=clubroom hasclub=yes
opens invite,share
feel smile
- [Welcome to our club room. It's a mess.|This room's like a second home.|We spend so much time in here.] [Don't look at the corner.|I have a drawer of snacks here.|Too much, maybe.]
- [The {club} needs new members, you know.|We're planning something for the festival.] [Hint, hint.|It's a secret.]
- [Everyone left their stuff everywhere again.|I'm the only one who cleans in here.] [Typical.|Not fair.]

@rule small.place.clubroom.rain
on small
when subject=place placeid=clubroom wet=yes
opens share,invite
- [Rainy days are club room days.|Everyone's in here because of the rain.|We made tea because of the rain.] [Cozy, right?|It's packed.|Want some?]
- [The windows are rattling.|Somebody's umbrella is dripping on my bag.] [I'm keeping the door shut.|Ugh.]
- [Rain means board games in the club room.|We're playing cards till it stops.] [Join us!|You in?]

# ---- anywhere: a fight on her mind, and the girl she can't stand nearby
@rule small.place.fight
on small
when subject=place fight=yes
opens comfort,ask
feel sad
- [Sorry, I'm not great company today.|I had a fight with {fightwho}.|My head's somewhere else.] [It's stupid.|We're not talking.|You noticed?]
- [Have you ever said something you couldn't take back?|{Fightwho} and I had a big one.] [Yeah. Me too, today.|It's been a bad week.]
- [I don't want to talk about {fightwho}.|I'm trying not to think about the fight.] [...Maybe later.|It's not working.]

@rule small.place.rivalnear
on small
when subject=place rivalnear=*
opens tease,ask
feel pout
- [Ugh, {rivalnear} is here.|Of all the people... {rivalnear}.|Don't look now, but {rivalnear} is staring.] [Let's go somewhere else.|Just ignore her.|Great.]
- [{Rivalnear} and I don't exactly get along.|Can we talk somewhere {rivalnear} isn't?] [Long story.|Please?]
- [If {rivalnear} says anything, I'm leaving.|I can feel {rivalnear} judging me.] [Fair warning.|Ignore it. I'm trying.]
